span></span> </h3> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">9</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td colspan="2" style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">Strong adhesive strength</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">%</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">≤</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">20</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">---</span></span></span> </h3> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">10</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td colspan="2" style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">Aluminum-plate thickness</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">OD</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">≥</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">2.0</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">---</span></span></span> </h3> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">11</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td colspan="2" style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">Aluminum-plate equality</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">%</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">±</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">15</span></span></span> </h3> </td> <td style="text-align:left;color:#000000;font-family:inherit;font-size:9pt;" valign="middle"> <h3 style="color:red;"> <span style="font-size:16px;"><span style="font-family:Tahoma;"><span style="line-height:normal;vertical-align:baseline;">---</span></span></span> </h3> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> <h3 style=''text-align:left;color:red;text-indent:0px;font-family:"font-style:normal;background-color:#FFFFFF;''> </h3>', '2026-09-06 20:58:45');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO cms_items (c_id, i_id, title, pic, content, addtime) VALUES (73, 262, 'BOPET metalized film (Polyester metallized film )', '../upload/image/20180826/20180826204843_53003.jpg', '<p></p><p align="left" style="color:#59595B;text-indent:20pt;font-family:宋体;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;background-color:#FFFFFF;"> <span style="color:#E53333;font-family:Tahoma;font-size:18px;">BOPET metalized film (Polyester metallized film )</span></p> <p align="left" style="color:#59595B;text-indent:20pt;font-family:宋体;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;background-color:#FFFFFF;"> <span style="color:#E53333;font-family:Tahoma;font-size:18px;">Color : Silver metallized</span></p> <p align="left" style="color:#59595B;text-indent:20pt;font-family:宋体;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;background-color:#FFFFFF;"> <span style="color:#E53333;font-family:Tahoma;font-size:18px;">Thickness : 1.5,3.8,4.5,6.0,8.0,10.0,12,14,15,25,50,75,150,185,250,380,450…Microns</span></p> <p align="left" style="color:#59595B;text-indent:20pt;font-family:宋体;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;background-color:#FFFFFF;"> <span style="color:#E53333;font-family:Tahoma;font-size:18px;">Width :95-1800MM</span></p> <p align="left" style="color:#59595B;text-indent:20pt;font-family:宋体;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;background-color:#FFFFFF;"> <span style="color:#E53333;font-family:Tahoma;font-size:18px;">Length :6000-36000M</span></p> <p align="left" style="color:#59595B;text-indent:20pt;font-family:宋体;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;background-color:#FFFFFF;"> <span style="color:#E53333;font-family:Tahoma;font-size:18px;">Inner core :3”(76MM),6”(76MM).</span></p> <p align="left" style="color:#59595B;text-indent:20pt;font-family:宋体;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;background-color:#FFFFFF;"> <span style="color:#E53333;font-family:Tahoma;font-size:18px;">Applications: used for packaging ,lamination ,and so forth.</span></p>', '2026-09-06 20:58:45');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO cms_items (c_id, i_id, title, pic, content, addtime) VALUES (73, 504, '4.0-4.5 Microns vacuum aluminum metallized polyester BOPET film silver', '../upload/image/20260223/20260223173016_39451.jpg', '<p>4.0-4.5 Microns vacuum aluminum metallized polyester BOPET film silver&nbsp;<br/> 4.0-4.5Microns vacuum aluminum metallized polyester BOPET film silver for printing &amp; lamination.&nbsp;<br/> Thickness of BOPET polyester basic film: 4.0,4.2,4.3,4.4,4.5,4.55,4.6,4.8,5.0,5.7,6.0um&nbsp;<br/> thcikenss of the vacuum aluminum metallized layer : 0.005-0.01microns<br/> width of BOPET polyester basic film: 910,902,935,980,1010,1020,1030,1050,1110,1260,1300,1480mm<br/> length of 4.5Microns vacuum aluminum metallized polyester:15000,18500,20000,24000,36000m&nbsp;<br/> feature of 4.5Microns vacuum aluminum metallized polyester: silver metallized<br/> 4.0-4.5Microns vacuum aluminum metallized polyester BOPET film silver, unprinting &amp;&nbsp; uncoating ( for priting and laminating) ,<br/> have stability features in metallized application and thickness stability,in good heat resistance,easy processing in laminating<br/> Our company (Asia pacific industry group) offer ?4.0-4.5Microns vacuum aluminum metallized polyester BOPET film products to the world market sufficiently.&nbsp;<br/> <p>H.S CODE of 4.0-4.5Microns polyester BOPET vacuum aluminum metallized film: 3920620000</p> <p><img src="../upload/image/no-photo.png" alt="" /></p> <p><img src="../upload/image/no-photo.png" alt="" /></p>', '2026-09-06 20:58:46');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO cms_items (c_id, i_id, title, pic, content, addtime) VALUES (73, 505, '4.5Microns polyester VM-BOPET metallized film', '../upload/image/20260223/20260223173005_59169.jpg', '<p>4.5Microns polyester VM-BOPET metallized film<br/> features: high tensile strength, good oxygen barrier property, high definition and gloss, and excellent dimensional stability, good flatness, good ink adhesion, excellent dimensional<br/> stability and workability.<br/> usage/application: printing &amp; laminating.<br/> a.) suitable for printing machinery, and higher adaptability of high-speed printing machinery&nbsp;<br/> b.) laminating: able to compound with paper, card, pe, bopa, bopp films and other materials.<br/> c.) stock lot films widely used in paper lamination<br/> d.) surface treatment: corona one side or corona two sides.<br/> e.) specifications and dimensions; 4.5-4.55mic*620-1,485mm*12,000-36,000m*6"core<br/> <br/> <p><img src="../upload/image/no-photo.png" alt="" /></p> <p><img src="../upload/image/no-photo.png" alt="" /></p>', '2026-09-06 20:58:46');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO cms_items (c_id, i_id, title, pic, content, addtime) VALUES (73, 508, 'Vacuum Aluminum Metallized 4.5 Micron BOPET polyester Film', '../upload/image/20260307/20260307110158_88579.jpg', '<p><strong><span style="color:#009900;">Vacuum Aluminum Metallized 4.5 Micron BOPET polyester Film</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">Vacuum aluminum metallized 4.5-micron (4.5um) BOPET (VMPET) is a high-performance, ultra-thin specialty material.&nbsp;</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">In this configuration, the 4.5µm polyester base provides the structural carrier, while a nanometer-scale layer of vaporized aluminum provides high-reflectivity and barrier properties.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">Here is a detailed breakdown of its properties, applications, and technical significance.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">1. Key Technical PropertiesUltra-Thin Gauge: At 4.5 microns, it is one of the thinnest commercially available metallized films.&nbsp;</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">This allows for maximum "yield" (more square meters per kilogram of material).</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">High Barrier Performance: The aluminum layer significantly reduces the Oxygen Transmission Rate (OTR) and Water Vapor Transmission Rate (WVTR) compared to clear film.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">Thermal Stability: As a BOPET-based material, it maintains dimensional stability at highertemperatures (melting point ≈ 260° C), which is critical for heat-sealing and high-speedlamination.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">Optical Density (OD): Typically ranges from 1.8 to 2.5. This determines the "brightness"and opacity of the silver finish.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">High Tensile Strength: Despite its thinness, the biaxial orientation gives it the mechanicalstrength to be processed on industrial coating and slitting machines without stretching orsnapping</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">2. Primary Applications</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">A. Thermal Transfer Ribbons (TTR) - Premium Grade</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">The Role: Metallized 4.5um BOPET is often used as the base for high-end resin or wax-resin ribbons.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">The Benefit: The metallization can act as a "heat-shield" or a primer layer that improvesthe release of the ink and protects the print head from overheating.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">B. High-Performance Lamination (Flexible Packaging)</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">The Role: It acts as the middle barrier layer in a multi-layer structure (e.g.,BOPP /VMPET 4.5m / PE).</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">The Benefit: It provides the barrier of a much thicker film while keeping the totalpackaging weight extremely low. This is ideal for snack food pouches and "lightweighting"initiatives.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">C. Insulation &amp; Electronics</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">The Role: Used in Cryogenic Insulation (multi-layer insulation or MLI) and radiantbarriers.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">The Benefit: The silver surface reflects up to 98% of radiant heat. Its ultra-thin natureallows for many layers to be wrapped in a small space (crucial for aerospace and LNG tankinsulation).</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">Capacitors: Some ultra-thin metallized BOPET is used in the manufacturing of filmcapacitors.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">D. Decorative &amp; Yarn Applications</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">The Role: Slit into tiny strips to create Metallic Yarn (Lurex) for textiles.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">The Benefit: Provides high shine and metallic luster while remaining soft enough to bewoven into fabrics.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">3. Comparison: Metallized vs. Aluminum Foil</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">4. Technical Keywords for Sourcing</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">When communicating with suppliers (like Shuangxing, Toray, or CloudFilm), use thesespecific terms:</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">VMPET 4.5mic: Short for Vacuum Metallized PET.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">Metal Bond Strength: The force required to peel the aluminum from the PET (crucial forlamination).</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">&nbsp;Dyne Level: Usually needs to be &gt; 42 dyne for lamination adhesive to stick.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">&nbsp;Yield (m2/kg): For 4.5uum, the yield is approximately 158 m2/kg.</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">Pro-Tip for Purchasing:</span></strong><br/> <strong><span style="color:#009900;">If you are buying 4.5um Metallized Off-grade (Substandard), it is excellent for paper-to-cardboard lamination (like luxury cigarette or liquor boxes). The paper provides the strength,and the "substandard" metallization still provides 100% of the required metallic aesthetic for amuch lower price.</span></strong></p>', '2026-09-06 20:58:46');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO cms_items (c_id, i_id, title, pic, content, addtime) VALUES (73, 509, '6 Microns Metallized BOPET Film', '../upload/image/20260307/20260307110315_79491.jpg', '<p><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family:&quot;color:#878D95;font-size:14px;"> <b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">6 Microns Metallized BOPET Film</span></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family:&quot;color:#878D95;font-size:14px;"> <span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">6 microns (often written as 6um) represents one of the thinnest commercially available gauges for&nbsp;</span><b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Biaxially-oriented Polyethylene Terephthalate</span></b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">&nbsp;(BOPET) film. When this ultra-thin substrate is "metallized"—usually with a microscopic layer of high-purity aluminum—it becomes a high-performance material used primarily in specialized industrial and packaging applications.</span></p> <div class="MsoNormal" align="center" style="margin:0px auto;padding:0px;font-family:&quot;color:#878D95;font-size:14px;text-align:center;"> <hr /> </div> <p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family:&quot;color:#878D95;font-size:14px;"> <b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Key Technical Specifications</span></b></p> <table class="MsoNormalTable ke-zeroborder" border="0" cellpadding="0" style="margin:0px auto;padding:0px;font-family:&quot;color:#878D95;font-size:14px;"> <tbody> <tr> <td style="font-family:&quot;"> <p class="MsoNormal"> <b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Property</span></b></p> </td> <td style="font-family:&quot;"> <p class="MsoNormal"> <b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Typical Value / Description</span></b></p> </td> </tr> </tbody> <tbody> <tr> <td style="font-family:&quot;"> <p class="MsoNormal"> <b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Thickness</span></b></p> </td> <td style="font-family:&quot;"> <p class="MsoNormal"> <span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">6um (0.006mm/24 gauge)</span></p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="font-family:&quot;"> <p class="MsoNormal"> <b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Material</span></b></p> </td> <td style="font-family:&quot;"> <p class="MsoNormal"> <span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Polyester (PET) resin stretched in two directions</span></p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="font-family:&quot;"> <p class="MsoNormal"> <b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Metallization</span></b></p> </td> <td style="font-family:&quot;"> <p class="MsoNormal"> <span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Vacuum-deposited Aluminum (VMPET)</span></p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="font-family:&quot;"> <p class="MsoNormal"> <b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Optical Density</span></b></p> </td> <td style="font-family:&quot;"> <p class="MsoNormal"> <span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Typically&nbsp;</span><b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">2.0 to 2.8</span></b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">&nbsp;(Adjustable based on barrier needs)</span></p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="font-family:&quot;"> <p class="MsoNormal"> <b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Surface Tension</span></b></p> </td> <td style="font-family:&quot;"> <p class="MsoNormal"> <span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">&gt;40 dynes/cm (Standard for printing/lamination)</span></p> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <div class="MsoNormal" align="center" style="margin:0px auto;padding:0px;font-family:&quot;color:#878D95;font-size:14px;text-align:center;"> <hr /> </div> <p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family:&quot;color:#878D95;font-size:14px;"> <b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Core Advantages</span></b></p> <ul style="font-family:&quot;color:#878D95;font-size:14px;"> <li class="MsoNormal"> <b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">Superior Yield:</span></b><span style="color:#009900;font-size:18px;">&nbsp;Because it is so thin, 6-micron film provides a much higher "square-meter-per-kilogram" yield compared to standard 10 or 12-micron films, making it highly cost-effective for high-volume runs.</span>', '2026-09-06 20:58:46');